Encapsulation is the process of wrapping data and the methods that operate on that data into a single unit (a class) while restricting direct access to the data. In Java, it is achieved by making variables private and providing controlled access through public methods such as getters, setters, or other business methods. Encapsulation improves data security, validation, maintainability, and flexibility.

