Parameterized Constructor -
	A parameterized constructor is a constructor that accepts one or more parameters. It is used to initialize an object's instance variables with specific values at the time of object creation.
	
A parameterized constructor is a constructor that accepts one or more parameters and is used to initialize an object's instance variables with specific values at the time of object creation. It allows different objects to be created with different initial states.

